    action: "If the M.2 riser is embedded on the system board, create an HPE Support Case. \n 1. Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to \nhttps://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click **Warranty Status**.\n\nThis enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service guide.\n\n 2. Under **Support Cases**, click **Access Cases**, and then create a support case. \nHPE Support will contact you.\n\nIf the M.2 riser is on a removable board, locate and reseat it. See the server maintenance and service guide for more information. \nFor more information, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website:\n\nHPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)\nHPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)",
