    symptom: "%1 Configuration Error: The system has exceeded the installed energy pack capacity.",
    cause: "Possible causes:\n\nThere are too many controllers and/or NVDIMMs for the energy pack to support.\nThe energy pack is unsupported on this server.\nSystem ROM, Smart Array and management processor firmware are updated.\nThe energy pack is faulty.",
    action: "1. Ensure the storage controller and NVDIMM configuration is supported in the server.\n2. Update the System ROM, Smart Array, and iLO firmware. \nService Pack for ProLiant (SPP) contains server drivers, systems software, and firmware. For more information about SPP, see the SPP website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Each SPP has an accompanying server support guide that lists the supported servers and components available for each of the supported servers. The server support guides and Service Pack for ProLiant Quick Start Guide are available on the SPP Information Library (http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation).\n\nTo update firmware on HPE Apollo and HPE ProLiant products, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide and the SUM Best Practices Planning Guide at http://www.hpe.com/info/SmartUpdate/docs. The SPP uses Smart Update Manager (SUM) to deploy firmware and system software components.\n\nTo update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the HPE Synergy Firmware Update Overview at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.\n\n3. To confirm energy pack status in the iLO GUI, click **System Information** in the iLO GUI navigation tree. \nFor more information, see the iLO User Guide at http://www.hpe.com/support/ilo-docs.\n\n4. To install a Smart Storage battery with capacity to support all installed battery-back devices, such as array controllers or NVDIMMs, create an HPE Support Case.",
