    action: "Install a new processor that supports the configured AMP mode. This must be done by an authorized service provider.\n\n**Caution**: When reducing the server to a minimum configuration for troubleshooting, do not remove additional processors. Processors and heatsinks are not designated for customer self-repair. The processor and heatsink must be removed and replaced by a support specialist.\n\nBefore performing any troubleshooting steps that involve processors, review the following guidelines:\n\nBe sure that only authorized personnel perform the troubleshooting steps that involve installation, removal, or replacement of a processor.\nAlways complete all other troubleshooting procedures before an support specialist removes or replaces a processor.\n\nFor more information, see the troubleshooting guide for your product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website:\n\nHPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/gen10-troubleshooting)\nHPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-troubleshooting)\n\nCreate an HPE Support Case.\n\n1. Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to \nhttps://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click **Warranty Status**.\n\nThis enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service guide.\n\n2. Under **Support Cases**, click **Access Cases**, and then create a support case. \nHPE Support will contact you.",
