    title: "NVDIMMs have been removed from Processor %1. All NVDIMMs on Processor %2 have been disabled",
    symptom: "NVDIMMs have been removed from Processor %1. All NVDIMMs on Processor %2 have been disabled.",
    cause: "One or more NVDIMMs were removed from the identified processor. The removed NVDIMMs were part of an existing interleaved NVDIMM set. Removal of any NVDIMM from an existing functional interleaved set breaks the functionality of entire set.",
    action: "To continue to use the previously functioning interleaved set, reinstall the NVDIMM.\n\n1. Disconnect each power cord from the power source.\n2. Disconnect each power cord from the server.\n3. Remove the NVDIMM. \n**CAUTION**: Failure to properly handle NVDIMMs can cause damage to NVDIMM components and the system board connector. See the Best Practices for Handling Memory Modules in ProLiant Server Configurations ( http://h20564.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docId=emr_na-c00868283).\n\n4. Clean the NVDIMM and the NVDIMM slot with anti-static compressed air.\n5. Reinstall the NVDIMM.",
