    title: "Slot encryption failure: Encrypted logical drives might be offline",
    symptom: "Master Key is incorrect on or not retrieved from Remote Key Manager. Encrypted logical drives may be offline. System may not boot.",
    cause: "The management processor is unable to communicate with the Remote Key License Server due to a network or configuration issue. SmartArray Drive Encryption cannot get the authentication keys to decrypt the drives.",
    action: "1. Check the network connection between the iLO management port and the remote key manager.\n2. Verify that the remote key manager configuration settings in iLO are properly configured.\n3. If the issue persists, update the iLO, Smart Array, and System ROM to the latest versions. \nTo update the firmware on HPE ProLiant servers, see Keeping the system current in the Troubleshooting Guide for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers at http://www.hpe.com/info/Gen10-troubleshooting.\n\nTo update the firmware on HPE Synergy products, see the Best Practices for HPE Synergy Firmware and Driver Updates at http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs.",
