    action: "1. Be sure no loose connections exist. For more information, see the _Resolving loose connections_ section in the Troubleshooting Guide for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers at http://www.hpe.com/info/Gen10-troubleshooting.\n2. Be sure the drive or backplane is cabled properly.\n3. Be sure the drive data cable is working by replacing it with a known functional cable.\n4. Be sure drive blanks are installed properly when the server is operating. Drives may overheat and cause sluggish response or drive failure.\n5. Set drive to Unconfigured Good.\n6. Verify backplane, controller, RAID config, and drive compatibility.\n7. Power cycle the server. If the drive shows up, check to see if the drive firmware needs to be updated.",
