    cause: "The enabling of encryption for the PMEM device failed due to encryption logic.",
    action: "1. Retry encryption enablement with the correct passphrase. \n 1. Reboot the system, and then press **F9** when the POST screen is displayed.\n 2. Press **F9**. \nThe **System Utilities** page is displayed.\n\n 3. Select **BIOS/Platform Configuration (RBSU)**.\n 4. Select **Server Security**.\n 5. Select **Device Encryption Options**.\n 6. Select **Device Encryption Settings**.\n 7. Select **Encrypted Devices**.\n 8. Select appropriate device under **Select Device**.\n 9. Select **Modify Passphrase** in the **Select Operation** box.\n 10. Select **Auto** or **Manual** in the **Passphrase Type** box.\n 11. If using **Manual Passphrase Type**, enter your passphrase in the **Passphrase** box.\n 12. Click **Start Operation**.",
