    symptom: "Backup power is not available for DIMM Slot belonging to Processor %1, DIMM %2 (SN:%3-%4-%5-%6). Future backups are not possible. Data from the last successful backup is intact, but data modified after the last successful backup will be lost if power cannot be restored.",
    cause: "The backup energy source is used to provide power to the NVDIMM-N modules in case of a system power loss. Data in the NVDIMM-N volatile memory must be backed up to the non-volatile flash storage prior to removing power to the NVDIMM-N. If the backup energy source goes bad or becomes disconnected, the backup is not performed, and any modified data since the last backup is lost.",
    action: "1. Backup NVDIMM contents to other media to preserve data.\n2. Verify that the backup energy source is properly installed.\n3. Allow two hours for backup energy source to charge.\n4. Confirm backup energy source status.\n5. Contact support if the condition persists.",
