    event: 0x0009,
    title: "Network adapter link down (Chassis %1, Slot %2, Port %3)",
    symptom: "Network adapter link down (Chassis %1, Slot %2, Port %3)",
    cause: "Possible causes:\n\n1. The firmware or drivers are outdated, mismatched, or faulty.\n2. The NIC or cable is not seated properly.\n3. The NIC, the cable, or other hardware is faulty.\n4. The hardware components are not supported in the same configuration.\n5. The NIC is not supported on the server.",
    action: "Refer to the NIC issues flowchart in the Troubleshooting Guide for HPE ProLiant Gen10 servers.\n\n1. Be sure both ends of cable are connected and not loose.\n2. Go to the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Support website to verify and install available updates for the following: \nAdapter firmware\nAdapter driver\nSystem ROM.\n\n3. Be sure the device at the other end of the connection is on and functioning properly.\n4. Be sure the network port is not disabled in the operating system.\n5. Use a different cable, a different port on the switch, or use a different switch.",
    severity: "warning",
    category: "network",
    platforms: ["Gen10","Gen10 Plus","Gen11","Gen12"],
