    symptom: "Smart Array: SSD wear status level changed.",
    cause: "SSD Wear Status Level has changed to one of the following:\n\n1. Unknown\n2. Ok\n3. 56 Days Remaining\n4. 5 Percent Remaining\n5. 2 Percent Remaining\n6. SSD Wear Out. Drive will indicate a predictive failure alert.",
    action: "Depending on usage patterns and business requirements, prepare to replace drive or modify workloads.\n\nReplace the device if indicated. For more information, see the server maintenance and service guide on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website.\n\n1. Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to the: \nCustomer Self Repair website.\n\nThis enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service guide.\n\n2. Create a support case at: http://www.hpe.com/support/hpesc. \nHPE Support will contact you.",
