    event: 0x0213,
    title: "Unsupported DIMM configuration detected",
    symptom: "A POST message displays: Unsupported DIMM configuration detected - Processor %1 DIMM %2. The DIMM has more ranks than is supported by this system. (Major Code:%3, Minor Code:%4).",
    cause: "An unsupported DIMM is installed in the server.",
    action: "Replace the identified DIMM with a supported DIMM.\n\n1. Remove all power. \n 1. Disconnect each power cord from the power source.\n 2. Disconnect each power cord from the server\n\n2. Remove the DIMM. \n**CAUTION**: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at: http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs\n\n3. Install the new DIMM.",
    severity: "warning",
    category: "memory",
    platforms: ["Gen10","Gen10 Plus","Gen11","Gen12"],
    doc: "ilogen12-msg-en_us",
    url: "https://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/docDisplay?docId=ilogen12-msg-en_us&page=class0x0032code0x0213-gen12.html&docLocale=en_US",
