    symptom: "A POST message displays: The System ROM image could not be authenticated or recovered.",
    cause: "The System ROM image is corrupt or invalid.",
    action: "Update the System ROM to restore system operation.\n\nThere are multiple ways to upgrade the firmware:\n\nHPE Support website:\n\n1. Go to https://www.hpe.com/us/en/support.html.\n2. Click **HPE Storage, Servers and Networking**.\n3. Enter product name, and then click **Go**.\n4. Click **Get drivers, software, and firmware**.\n5. Select the appropriate operating system.\n6. Select the appropriate patch, and then click Download.\n\nSmart Update Manager (SUM):\n\n1. Download SUM from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/sum).\n2. Be sure you have the latest SPP (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp/download).\n3. Open SUM and add the baseline that includes the Smart Array driver. For specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http://www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.\n\nSmart Update Tool (SUT):\n\n**Note**: To use SUT, you must have HPE OneView downloaded and installed. For more information, see the HPE OneView documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/ovvcenter/docs.\n\n1. Download SUT from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/info/hpsut).\n2. Be sure you have the latest SPP (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp/download).\n3. Run SUT from the command line (On-Demand mode) to update the Smart Array firmware. For more information, see to the HP SUT documents at http://www.hpe.com/info/sut-docs.\n\nService Pack for ProLiant (SPP):\n\nUpdate the Smart Array firmware by downloading the SPP from the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website (http://www.hpe.com/servers/spp). Refer to the SPP documentation at http://www.hpe.com/info/spp/documentation for instructions on updating the firmware.\n\n**Note**: Downloading an SPP requires a contract with Hewlett Packard Enterprise and an HPE Passport ID. If you do not have an HPE Passport ID, go to http://www.hpe.com/info/insightonline.\n\n**Note**: Downloading the entire SPP can take a significant amount of time.\n\nOnline Flash components\n\nThis component provides updated system firmware that can be installed directly on supported operating systems. Additionally, when used in conjunction with the SUM, this Smart Component allows you to update firmware on remote servers from a central location.\n\nThis remote deployment capability eliminates the need for you to be physically present at the server to perform a firmware update.\n\nFor specific instructions on updating firmware, see the Smart Update Manager User Guide, at http://www.hpe.com/info/hpsum/documentation.",
