    cause: "The indicated Intel Optane PMem for HPE Module is not installed on the first memory controller of that processor socket. This memory controller must be populated with PMEMs before any other memory controllers on the socket.",
    action: "Install Intel PMEM in DIMM slot %1 before populating other slots with PMEM per the memory population guidelines. Review documentation for more information on supported configurations.\n\nFor more information, see the server maintenance and service guide for your product on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise website:\n\nHPE ProLiant Gen10 (http://www.hpe.com/info/proliantgen10-docs)\nHPE Synergy (http://www.hpe.com/info/synergy-docs)\n\n1. Remove all power. \n 1. Disconnect each power cord from the power source.\n 2. Disconnect each power cord from the server\n\n2. **CAUTION**: Failure to properly handle DIMMs can cause damage to DIMM components and the system board connector. See the DIMM handling guidelines on the Hewlett Packard Enterprise Library at: http://www.hpe.com/info/enterprise/docs\n\n3. Install the DCPMMs.\n\nIf this issue persists create an HPE Support Case.\n\n1. Verify the component is either under warranty or contract. Go to \nhttps://support.hpe.com/hpesc/public/home, and then click **Warranty Check**.\n\nThis enables HPE to ship replacement parts directly to you once a failure has been confirmed. For specific information about customer replaceable parts, refer to the product maintenance and service guide.\n\n2. Under **Support Cases**, click **Access Cases**, and then create a support case. \nHPE Support will contact you.",
